alse,"user_input_order":34}},{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_04e06a9245aac484016ae154911d408191a2def7780a7abb97","status":"completed","call_id":"call_ea9c023e24ad4afabd579a2f322004c1","name":"exec","input":"text(ALL_TOOLS.filter(x=>/search|browse|web/i.test(x.name+\" \"+x.description)).map(x=>({name:x.name,description:x.description.slice(0,170)})).slice(0,70));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18032-3452-7b43-8fac-481146db9710","create_time":1793152145.3603487}},{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18032-5ab6-7213-ad59-e84151e257d2","call_id":"call_ea9c023e24ad4afabd579a2f322004c1","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"[{\"name\":\"list_mcp_resource_templates\",\"description\":\"Lists resource templates provided by MCP servers. Parameterized resource templates allow servers to share data that takes parameters and provides context to language mode\"},{\"name\":\"list_mcp_resources\",\"description\":\"Lists resources provided by MCP servers. Resources allow servers to share data that provides context to language models, such as files, database schemas, or application-s\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_app__open_in_codex\",\"description\":\"Show a workspace file, browser tab, terminal, or review in a Codex panel. The calling thread in the calling window receives the tab by default. Set threadId only when the\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__hotline_get_local_hotline\",\"description\":\"Look up local helpline information for the user based on country inferred from the conversation. You must use this tool before providing a suicide or self-harm helpline; \"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__pets_prepare_pet_upload\",\"description\":\"Prepare a user-scoped ChatGPT pet sprite-sheet upload. First call validate_pet_spritesheet and repair all reported errors. Pass the final sprite sheet's absolute local pa\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__pets_validate_pet_spritesheet\",\"description\":\"Validate a ChatGPT pet PNG or WebP before creating an upload session. Pass its absolute local path as file; the host uploads and rewrites it before this tool receives the\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__plugin_management_get_app_permissions\",\"description\":\"Inspect one named ChatGPT plugin's global/default and plugin-specific permission settings. Use when the user asks what the plugin may read, write, or do, whether it must \"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__plugin_management_get_plugin_dependencies\",\"description\":\"Resolve the canonical public plugins declared by one plugin's app manifest. Use only when a skill or user explicitly asks for dependency metadata. Pass a plugin ID or nam\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__plugin_management_search_plugins\",\"description\":\"Search available plugins when the user explicitly requests a plugin or provider, or when their task would benefit from an external app, account, service, data source, or \"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__plugin_management_suggest_plugins\",\"description\":\"Suggest plugins when an external integration would help the user. The user does not need to mention plugins or installation. Call plugin_management.search_plugins for rel\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__plugin_management_uninstall_app\",\"description\":\"Uninstall ChatGPT plugins only for explicit uninstall, remove, or disconnect intent. Pass every exact, user-approved target in one call. For a missing/broad target such a\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__plugin_management_update_app_permissions\",\"description\":\"Update global ChatGPT plugin permissions or a plugin-specific override. Omit app_id for global-only updates and provide it for plugin-specific updates. Map Always ask to \"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__search_service_web_run\",\"description\":\"Run the web commands documented in this namespace.\\n\\nTool for accessing the internet.\\n\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Examples of different commands available in this tool\\n\\nExamples of differen\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__sites_add_custom_domain\",\"description\":\"Add a custom domain to a published site. The response includes a CNAME target for subdomains, A record targets for zone apex domains, and all App Garden and Cloudflare va\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__sites_change_site_slug\",\"description\":\"Change a site's public URL label. The change runs asynchronously. When the result is pending, use get_site to observe the current slug; do not call this mutation again to\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__sites_create_schedule\",\"description\":\"Create and link a cloud task for a published Site when the user has requested scheduling. Before creating a new schedule, read get_site. If automations is missing or null\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__sites_create_site\",\"description\":\"Create a site only when .openai/hosting.json has no project_id. If it has one, reuse that site. Never call this tool more than once for the same local site. This tool doe\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__sites_create_source_repository_write_credential\",\"description\":\"Create a short-lived source repository write credential when the credential returned by create_site is missing or no longer usable. It authorizes Git pushes to the site's\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__sites_deploy_private_site_version\",\"description\":\"Deploy a saved site version to production for a site created in the current flow whose owner-only access has not changed, or an existing site already known to be owner-pr\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__sites_deploy_site_version\",\"description\":\"Deploy a saved site version to production when the site is shared, public, cannot be verified as owner-only, or private deployment is unavailable. For existing sites not \"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__sites_generate_siwc_bypass_token\",\"description\":\"Generate a bearer token for identity-less API requests that bypasses a site's Sign in with ChatGPT gate. Call this explicit token tool only when the user asks for a bypas\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__sites_get_deployment_status\",\"description\":\"Get the current status of a production deployment. Only poll when a deployment ID is available; the deployment owns its saved version, so do not supply version_id. Contin\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__sites_get_environment_variables\",\"description\":\"Get the production runtime environment variables for a site. These values are separate from local .env files and .openai/hosting.json. This tool is part of plugin `Sites`\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__sites_get_site\",\"description\":\"Get a site and its current access configuration, including external visitors. For a Library Site result, copy its server-returned site_metadata.project_id unchanged as pr\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__sites_get_site_version\",\"description\":\"Get a saved site version and its source provenance. Retain version_id for follow-up calls, but report the user-facing version number when possible. This tool is part of p\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__sites_get_site_worker_logs\",\"description\":\"Read recent production Cloudflare Worker logs for a Site when diagnosing why a deployed website is crashing, returning an error, or failing after a click or tap. Resolve \"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__sites_list_custom_domains\",\"description\":\"List custom domains attached to a site. This tool is part of plugin `Sites`.\\n\\nUse Sites to build or modify websites, including landing pages, portfolios, dashboards, port\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__sites_list_site_versions\",\"description\":\"List saved site versions in newest-first order for history, deployment, or rollback selection. Defaults to 20 versions; limit must be an integer from 1 to 50. For more ve\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__sites_list_sites\",\"description\":\"List Sites you own in the selected account, including personal accounts. Defaults to 20 Sites; limit must be an integer from 1 to 50. For more results, call list_sites ag\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__sites_read_database_overview\",\"description\":\"Inspect the user tables in a deployed site's live Cloudflare D1 database before reading rows. Returns only exact binding and table names that fit the bounded model respon\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__sites_read_database_table_rows\",\"description\":\"Read one bounded page of rows from a user table in a deployed site's live Cloudflare D1 database. Call read_database_overview first and pass exact binding and table names\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__sites_refresh_custom_domain_status\",\"description\":\"Refresh custom domain validation status for a site. This tool is part of plugin `Sites`.\\n\\nUse Sites to build or modify websites, including landing pages, portfolios, dash\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__sites_remove_custom_domain\",\"description\":\"Remove a custom domain from a site. This tool is part of plugin `Sites`.\\n\\nUse Sites to build or modify websites, including landing pages, portfolios, dashboards, portals,\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__sites_save_site_version\",\"description\":\"Save a version of the site's pushed source without deploying it. Full SHA of the pushed source commit. It must match the current HEAD of the site's configured remote sour\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__sites_save_version_and_deploy_private\",\"description\":\"For a site created in the current flow whose owner-only access has not changed, or an existing site already known to be owner-private for the selected account, use this i\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__sites_update_environment_variables\",\"description\":\"Update production runtime environment variables for a site. Only listed keys change; all others remain unchanged. Store runtime values in Sites, not .openai/hosting.json.\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__sites_update_site_access\",\"description\":\"Update who can visit a site only when the user asks to change access. Set access_mode only when the user explicitly requests a different audience; omit it for collaborato\"},{\"name\":\"mcp__codex_apps__sites_update_site_metadata\",\"description\":\"Update a site's display title. This does not change the site's public URL. This tool is part of plugin `Sites`.\\n\\nUse Sites to build or modify websites, including landing \"},{\"name\":\"web__run\",\"description\":\"Tool for accessing the internet.\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n## Examples of different commands available in this tool\\r\\n\\r\\nExamples of different commands available in this tool:\\r\\n* `search\"}]"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18032-3452-7b43-8fac-481146db9710","create_time":1793152146.102688},"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}},{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_04e06a9245aac484016ae1549553e081918b2bd7d0296a5e4e","status":"completed","call_id":"call_e27cd22b77ce4bf28eba60b06bffb7b0","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.web__run({search_query:[{q:\"Spanish validated system usability scale SUS Spanish version questionnaire Sevilla 2020\"}],response_length:\"short\"}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18032-3452-7b43-8fac-481146db9710","create_time":1793152149.3351307}},{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18032-74cb-7ba3-a53c-bbaba01fd9c0","call_id":"call_e27cd22b77ce4bf28eba60b06bffb7b0","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.8 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation. (https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33325828/)\nciteturn0search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.9 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; # Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation. ... Publication date: 2020 Dec 16 ...   * Magdalena Del Rocio Sevilla-Gonzalez ... The Spanish SUS questionnaire was validated by 10 experts in mobile app development.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nJMIR Human Factors - Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation (https://humanfactors.jmir.org/2020/4/e21161/)\nciteturn0search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.9 years ago; Crawled: last week; Magdalena Del Rocio Sevilla-Gonzalez^{1, 2, 3} ;   Lizbeth Moreno Loaeza^{3} ;   Laura Sofia Lazaro-Carrera^{3} ;   Brigette Bourguet Ramirez^{3} ;   Anabel Vázquez Rodríguez^{4} ;   María Luisa Peralta-Pedrero^{5} ;   Paloma Almeda-Valdes^{3, 6} ... Translation, Cross-Cultural Adaptation, and Validation of the Malay Version of the System Usability Scale Questionnaire for the Assessment of Mobile Apps. ... URL: https://www.usability.gov/how-to-and-tools/methods/system-usability-scale.html [accessed 2020-09-11] 13], there is no evidence of the validity and reliability process. ... Second, to achieve the forward translation, the original version of the SUS was translated into Spanish by 2 independent translators with an adequate understanding of the source language: one individual had a master’s degree in translation studies and the other was a professional certified in English language and linguistics whose native language was Spanish. ... In this study, a Spanish version of the SUS questionnaire was developed and validated. ... URL: https://www.who.int/goe/publications/goe_mhealth_web.pdf [accessed 2020-12-08]\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nJMIR Preprints #21161: System Usability Scale Questionnaire for the assessment of electronic tools: Development and validation of a Spanish version (https://preprints.jmir.org/preprint/21161/accepted)\nciteturn0search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6.0 years ago; Crawled: 3 months ago; Sevilla-Gonzalez M, Moreno-Loaeza L, Lazaro-Carrera LS, Bourguet-Ramírez B, Vázquez-Rodríguez A, Peralta-Pedrero ML, Almeda-Valdés P\n\nSpanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation ... ## System Usability Scale Questionnaire for the assessment of electronic tools: Development and validation of a Spanish version ... The Spanish SUS questionnaire was validated by 10 experts in mobile app development. ... The content validity index of the new Spanish SUS was good based on the rating of the relevance of items of 0.92.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSpanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation - PMC (https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7773510/)\nciteturn0search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.9 years ago; Crawled: 4 days ago; # Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation\n\n### Magdalena Del Rocio Sevilla-Gonzalez, MSc, PhD ... This is an open-access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution License (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), which permits unrestricted use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original work, first published in JMIR Human Factors, is properly cited. ... The System Usability Scale (SUS) proposed by Brooke [9] in 1986 is a widely used questionnaire to assess the usability of a system, such as standard operating system–based software interfaces, webpages, and mobile apps. ... In this study, a Spanish version of the SUS questionnaire was developed and validated.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUsability as a Premise of Quality: First Steps Towards the Validation of the System Usability Scale (SUS) into Spanish | Journal of Audiovisual Translation (https://jatjournal.org/index.php/jat/article/view/77)\nciteturn0search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6.8 years ago; Crawled: last month;   * Irene Tor-Carroggio Universitat Autònoma de Barcelona http://orcid.org/0000-0003-2924-014X ... usability, usability evaluation, SUS, system usability scale, Spanish, questionnaire translation, questionnaire validation ... Originally designed in English, it is available in some other languages, such as Persian and Greek but no validated version in Spanish can be found yet.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nJMIR Human Factors - Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation (https://humanfactors.jmir.org/2020/4/e21161/authors)\nciteturn0search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.9 years ago; Crawled: yesterday; # Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation\n\n## Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation ... Magdalena Del Rocio Sevilla-Gonzalez^{1, 2, 3} ;   Lizbeth Moreno Loaeza^{3} ;   Laura Sofia Lazaro-Carrera^{3} ;   Brigette Bourguet Ramirez^{3} ;   Anabel Vázquez Rodríguez^{4} ;   María Luisa Peralta-Pedrero^{5} ;   Paloma Almeda-Valdes^{3, 6}\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nJMIR Human Factors - Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation (https://humanfactors.jmir.org/2020/4/e21161/citations)\nciteturn0search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.9 years ago; Crawled: today; # Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation\n\n## Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation ... Magdalena Del Rocio Sevilla-Gonzalez^{1, 2, 3} ;   Lizbeth Moreno Loaeza^{3} ;   Laura Sofia Lazaro-Carrera^{3} ;   Brigette Bourguet Ramirez^{3} ;   Anabel Vázquez Rodríguez^{4} ;   María Luisa Peralta-Pedrero^{5} ;   Paloma Almeda-Valdes^{3, 6}\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSpanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation - ScienceDirect (https://www.sciencedirect.com/org/science/article/pii/S2292949520000395)\nciteturn0search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.9 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation ... The System Usability Scale (SUS) is a common metric used to assess the usability of a system, and it was initially developed in English. ... The Spanish SUS questionnaire was validated by 10 experts in mobile app development. ... The CVI (Table 1) and FVI (Table 2) of the new Spanish version of the SUS were calculated to be 0.92 and 0.94, respectively.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSG3._Bruno_Rios_-_Prueba_de_concepto (https://revistas.ulima.edu.pe/index.php/Interfases/article/download/6557/6883/30221?inline=1)\nciteturn0search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Preguntas del cuestionario SUS validadas al español ... Tomado de Sevilla-González et al. (2020).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nJMIR Preprints #21161: Translation, cross-cultural adaptation and validation of the System Usability Scale questionnaire for the assessment of electronic tools “SUS”, to a new Spanish version (https://preprints.jmir.org/preprint/21161/submitted)\nciteturn0search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6.4 years ago; Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Sevilla-Gonzalez M, Moreno-Loaeza L, Lazaro-Carrera LS, Bourguet-Ramírez B, Vázquez-Rodríguez A, Peralta-Pedrero ML, Almeda-Valdés P ... ## Translation, cross-cultural adaptation and validation of the System Usability Scale questionnaire for the assessment of electronic tools “SUS”, to a new Spanish version ... The Spanish SUS questionnaire was validated by 10 experts in mobile app development. ... According to Cronbach’s alpha test 0.81 IC95% (0.74 – 0.86), the translated scale is s a reliable tool for the assessment of the usability of electronic tools.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nJMIR Human Factors - Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation (https://humanfactors.jmir.org/2020/4/e21161/tweetations)\nciteturn0search10 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.9 years ago; Crawled: last month; Image: Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation\n\n# Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation ... Magdalena Del Rocio Sevilla-Gonzalez^{1, 2, 3} ;   Lizbeth Moreno Loaeza^{3} ;   Laura Sofia Lazaro-Carrera^{3} ;   Brigette Bourguet Ramirez^{3} ;   Anabel Vázquez Rodríguez^{4} ;   María Luisa Peralta-Pedrero^{5} ;   Paloma Almeda-Valdes^{3, 6}\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nJMIR Human Factors - Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation (https://humanfactors.jmir.org/2020/4/e21161/metrics)\nciteturn0search11 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.9 years ago; Crawled: yesterday; # Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation\n\n## Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment of Electronic Tools: Development and Validation ... Magdalena Del Rocio Sevilla-Gonzalez^{1, 2, 3} ;   Lizbeth Moreno Loaeza^{3} ;   Laura Sofia Lazaro-Carrera^{3} ;   Brigette Bourguet Ramirez^{3} ;   Anabel Vázquez Rodríguez^{4} ;   María Luisa Peralta-Pedrero^{5} ;   Paloma Almeda-Valdes^{3, 6}\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTYPE Original Research (https://zaguan.unizar.es/record/170231/files/texto_completo.pdf)\nciteturn0search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; In the absence of a formally published Spanish validation ... Memory Questionnaire (PRMQ-S), originally developed by (Smith \net al., 2000) and subsequently adapted and validated for Spanish- ... Spanish version of the System Usability Scale (SUS), created by (Brooke, ... populations by (Sevilla-Gonzalez et al., 2020).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDiseño, desarrollo y (https://riubu.ubu.es/bitstream/10259/9555/1/Yanez_Perez_Iraya-Tesis.pdf)\nciteturn0search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.8 years ago; For the quantitative strand of the research, the System Usability Scale (SUS, ... The Spanish \nversion of the questionnaire was used (Del Rocio Sevilla-Gonzalez et al., 2020). ... multiplied by 2.5 to obtain a scale ranging from 0 to 100.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUsability as a Premise of Quality: (https://ddd.uab.cat/pub/artpub/2019/216459/document.pdf)\nciteturn0search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; First Steps Towards the Validation of the System Usability Scale (SUS) into Spanish ... Lastly, some commentaries about the questionnaire design ... Spanish version of SUS\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSevilla-Gonzalez et al (https://pdfs.semanticscholar.org/efa7/7e1cf21b4bab9653c2194b7b4007528fbfb1.pdf)\nciteturn0search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; Spanish Version of the System Usability Scale for the Assessment ... Magdalena Del Rocio Sevilla-Gonzalez1,2,3, MSc, PhD; Lizbeth Moreno Loaeza3, MSc; Laura Sofia Lazaro-Carrera3, ... The Spanish SUS questionnaire was validated by 10 experts in mobile app development. ... (JMIR Hum Factors 2020;7(4):e21161) doi: 10.2196/21161 ... mHealth; usability; validation; System Usability Scale; Spanish\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPRE-PRINT COPY (https://roderic.uv.es/rest/api/core/bitstreams/2c779123-6ff8-494e-a060-2dcc410134ed/content)\nciteturn0search16 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9 months ago; were considered (CFI=.932, TLI=.898; RMSEA=.055, CI 90%= 0.047, 0.062), ... items in the structure of the SUS and propose a short version of the SUS to be ... Keywords: System Usability Scale, validity, reliability, method effects, Spanish,\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAntwerp, 25/08/2021 (https://u-pad.unimc.it/retrieve/handle/11393/299007/2a98993e-5120-4bb6-8a0d-c3104861a994/10%20Greco_Jankowska_JAT_special_issue_2019.pdf)\nciteturn0search17 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5.2 years ago; of the System Usability Scale (SUS) into Spanish ... the validation of the System Usability ... but no validated version in Spanish can be found yet. ... questionnaire ...  Irene.Tor@uab.cat, https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2924-014X\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPrueba de usabilidad (https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prueba_de_usabilidad)\nciteturn0search18 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 1.9 years ago; * SUS (System Usability Scale): es una herramienta rápida y fiable para medir la usabilidad. ... En 2023 se ha validado el cuestionario en español (10 ítems), así como una versión corta de 5 ítems ... «Psychometric Properties of the Spanish Full and Short Forms of the System Usability Scale (SUS): Detecting the Effect of Negatively Worded Items». ... ISBN 0-8058-3290-4.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSystem usability scale (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/System_usability_scale)\nciteturn0search19 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 7 months ago;  Standard version of the system usability scale ... The final SUS score can be computed with the following formula:${\\displaystyle SUS=2.5\\left(20+\\sum ({\\text{SUS01}},{\\text{SUS03}},{\\text{SUS05}},{\\text{SUS07}},{\\text{SUS09}})-\\sum ({\\text{SUS02}},{\\text{SUS04}},{\\text{SUS06}},{\\text{SUS08}},{\\text{SUS10}})\\right)}$ ... Because it yields a single score on a scale of 0–100, it can be used to compare even systems that are outwardly dissimilar. This one-dimensional aspect of the SUS is both a benefit and a drawback because the questionnaire is necessarily quite general. ... The factor structure of the system usability scale (PDF).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nQuestionnaire for User Interaction Satisfaction (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Questionnaire_for_User_Interaction_Satisfaction)\nciteturn0search20 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 11 months ago; The QUIS is currently at Version 7.0 with demographic questionnaire, a measure of overall system satisfaction along 6 scales, and measures of 9 specific interface factors. ... In addition to English, the QUIS 7.0 is currently available in the following languages: German, Italian, Portuguese (Brazilian), and Spanish. ... * System Usability Scale (SUS) ... The QUIS Version 7.0 is an updated and expanded version of the previously validated QUIS 5.5.\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18032-3452-7b43-8fac-481146db9710","create_time":1793152152.7792287},"guardian_metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}},{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_04e06a9245aac484016ae1549b240c819181c9bcea23b85bc8","status":"completed","call_id":"call_c7abadb0ba814551a2f9ea8c6ae1b475","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.web__run({open:[{ref_id:\"https://humanfactors.jmir.org/2020/4/e21161/\"}],response_length:\"long\"}));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a18032-3452-7b43-8fac-481146db9710","create_time":1793152155.1467912}},{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a18032-85b1-7af0-9d9b-18549f680afd","call_id":"call_c7abadb0ba814551a2f9ea8c